test-results/

# Phase 1 (FR-1.6): the IEM CLI response cache is a regenerable HTTP cache with
# per-fetch timestamps; the derived daily-high CSVs beside it ARE the committed
# ground-truth record and stay tracked.
data/weather_truth/cache/

# Phase 2 (FR-2.2): re-fetchable IEM MOS run cache (434 files / 30 MB). The
# normalized forecast_series_*.csv beside it is the committed artifact.
data/forecast_archive/cache/

# Phase 2 (FR-2.1): decoded GEFS member cache — regenerable from NOAA NODD.
data/ensemble/cache/

# VM decommission snapshot (2026-08-22): 197 MB of compressed archives pulled off
# the GCE instance money-printer-preschool-20260322 before it was stopped. The
# payload is deliberately untracked (too large for git history); the committed
# record of what it contains, where each piece came from, and its SHA-256 lives
# in vm_snapshot_2026_08_22/MANIFEST.md.
vm_snapshot_2026_08_22/archive/
# Working extraction of the VM snapshot archives — regenerable by untarring
# archive/*.tgz. The 27 daily reconcile runs are the one irreplaceable piece and
# are committed separately under vm_snapshot_2026_08_22/reconcile_record/.
vm_snapshot_2026_08_22/extracted/
